  "number": 551,
  "title": "Jesus, Savior, Pilot Me",
  "artist": "Traditional",
  "key": "G",
  "lyrics": [
    "[G]Jesus, Savior, [C]pilot [G]me",
    "Over [C]life's [D7]tempestuous [G]sea;",
    "[D7]Unknown waves before me [G]roll,",
    "[D7]Hiding rock and treacherous [G]shoal.",
    "[G]Chart and compass [C]come from [G]Thee;",
    "Jesus, [C]Savior, [D7]pilot [G]me.",
    "",
    "As a mother stills her child,",
    "thou canst hush the ocean wild;",
    "boisterous waves obey thy will,",
    "when thou sayest to them, \"Be still!\"",
    "Wondrous sovreign of the sea,",
    "Jesus, Savior, pilot me.",
    "",
    "When at last I near the shore,",
    "and the fearful breakers roar",
    "'twixt me and the peaceful rest,",
    "then, while leaning on thy breast,",
    "may I hear thee say to me,",
    "\"Fear not, I will pilot thee."
  ],
